        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Hey all,\r\n\r\nMy friends and I encountered an issue or two while playing and we would like some feedback. Someone was playing Expatriette couldn't play any cards from her hand because they were all limited ongoings/equipments already in play. We know there's no way to actually play them, but we wanted to know if she could activate her power, even if it meant nothing happened.  So:\r\n\r\nA.) Can this Expatriette still activate her innate power if there are cards in his hand, but they cannot be played? (E.g. If for some reason you wanted to activate the effect of one of Spite's \"PL626 Compound XI\" drug card.\r\nB.) Can her \"Play a card\" power still be activated if there are 0 cards in the player's hand? \r\n\r\nSimilarly, The Wraith's card \"Grappling Hook\" reads as follows: \r\n\"Destroy 1 ongoing or environment card.\r\n\r\nYou may draw a card.\"\r\n\r\nSo:\r\n\r\nC.) Could The Wraith play \"Grappling Hook\" from the hand if there were no ongoing or environment cards to destroy?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nThe Hootenanny Crew.\r\n\r\nPS: Spite's drug card reads as follows: \"Whenever a hero used a power, Spice deals them 2 Toxic damage and that hero's player discards the top 5 cards of their deck.\"",
